    <!--
      Spelled out rather than "°C" and "°F". At the size these segments are set,
      a degree ring is a speck and the two options differ by one letter.
    -->
    <!--
      Where the first guess came from. Said once, in General, because a reader
      who opens Settings and finds Fahrenheit already chosen is owed an
      explanation of who chose it - and because it is the answer to "why is this
      wrong", which is the only reason most people will ever come here.
    -->
    <!--
      Brought across from This Note and Orobos, and named as they name them. Not
      translated: they are the names of two specific palettes - one built on
      Hara's White, one on Adams' zone system - the way a typeface keeps its name.
    -->
    <string name="theme_pure_white" translatable="false">Pure White</string>
    <string name="theme_pure_black" translatable="false">Pure Black</string>

